# Country tax packs

A later country tax system plugs into the generic engine. Do **not** rebuild posting.

Per country, add later: a pack in `PACKS` (code, extra invoice fields, e-invoicing/filing flags), optional seed `TaxRate` rows the accountant owns, then enable with `reviewed: true`. `AE`/`GB` are rejected on purpose — no fixtures, no claimed compliance.

Already works without a pack: exclusive/inclusive, compound (tax-on-tax vs GST+PST in parallel), reverse charge, invoice-time withholding, recoverable/irrecoverable, valid-from/to. An org can create “UAE 5% VAT” as a rate today; that is configuration, not a UAE country pack.

A pack will not magically give you: payment-time WHT, place-of-supply matrices, Fatoora/PEPPOL/GST e-invoicing XML, VAT return filing. Those are extra services when a named jurisdiction is chosen.
